hacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/727968555be54b474fcb51b972dc24c50ca7afe972d0cea5bae63f4d4db32888.png" 13194139534734 true] [17592186306456 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534734 true] [17592186306456 1111 #uuid "2aa1de9f-8d34-54d3-b400-53989df04305" 13194139534734 true] [17592186306457 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/0075556b1e97d2c805490deec07f0efa39257ccfc2d99117c7bcbbfc413a0fbb.png" 13194139534734 true] [17592186306457 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534734 true] [17592186306457 1111 #uuid "1d524a99-f6b4-5543-9cb6-cd996f1e96e2" 13194139534734 true] [17592186306458 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/21828e2eb3d107ea12e90d715de9a3c1350e6fd95f03b321be7ab81a8824b065.png" 13194139534734 true] [17592186306458 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534734 true] [17592186306458 1111 #uuid "6c76a135-c828-5360-a0d2-8627561989ea" 13194139534734 true] [17592186306459 1017 #edb/ref 17592186306460 13194139534734 true] [17592186306459 1089 "q-119324" 13194139534734 true] [17592186306459 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534734 true] [17592186306459 1100 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point along the line $y=2,$ the slope field has a positive slope\n- At every point along the line $y=0,$ the slope field is horizontal\n- At every point along the line $y=-2,$ the slope field has a negative slope" 13194139534734 true] [17592186306459 1113 #uuid "302c2eb2-363c-5d38-a827-d5d5950356a3" 13194139534734 true] [17592186306459 1145 "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).\n$$\n\nThis is an autonomous equation because the right-hand side is a function of $y$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $y,$ the slope does not vary with $x.$ \n\nNow, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. Consider a point of the form $(x,2)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,2)}=-2<0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,2)$ is negative for any $x.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(x,2)$ is equal to $-2$ for any $x.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Consider a point of the form $(x,0)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,0)}=-0=0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,0)$ is horizontal for any $x.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Consider a point of the form $(x,-2)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,-2)}=-(-2)=2>0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,-2)$ is positive for any $x.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(x,-2)$ is equal to $2$ for any $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"\n\nWe can use this information to begin sketching the slope field, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/8fc0b5be5c9147c29410ff7a082316403302f2bce7ec25c665ab7ccc5bf90b0f.png)" 13194139534734 true] [17592186306460 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306461 13194139534734 true] [17592186306460 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306462 13194139534734 true] [17592186306460 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306463 13194139534734 true] [17592186306460 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306464 13194139534734 true] [17592186306460 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306465 13194139534734 true] [17592186306460 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534734 true] [17592186306460 1041 "selection" 13194139534734 true] [17592186306460 1104 #edb/ref 17592186306465 13194139534734 true] [17592186306460 1110 #uuid "a04f6688-573e-59b4-8ccb-b85a4e68b23d" 13194139534734 true] [17592186306461 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534734 true] [17592186306461 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534734 true] [17